<h3>Frequently Asked Questions:</h3>

<b>What is a suspension?</b><br/>
A suspension is a temporal removal from duties that is issued by a supervisor pending further investigation. This is not a punishment, simply a means of preventing any further issues.<br/><br/>

<b>What happens after I have been suspended?</b><br/>
A PM is made informing you of your suspension with a time, date and location of a incident that a supervisor believes was gross misconduct. A member of the internal affairs investigation team will begin gathering evidence and will ask you for a statement regarding the incident.<br/><br/>

<b>Can I dispute a suspension?</b><br/>
A suspension is not a punishment and there is no need to dispute it. A member of IA will look over the alleged incident and you will be notified on what is happening from then. You will be notified when the suspension has been lifted.